{"severity":"CRITICAL","confidence":8,"path":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Views/VCSToolbar.swift","line":138,"category":"feedback","summary":"Clicking \"Try Again\" produces no visible change at all, so the one enabled control on this tier reads as dead. `model.refresh(force: true)` sets `state = .loading` — which nothing in VCSToolbar renders — and the presentation's `activity` is derived solely from `model.activeAction` (action-only), so no \"…\" title and no `ProgressView` appears (`isRunning` is `title?.hasSuffix(\"…\")`, false for \"Try Again\"; the spinner branch also requires `action != nil`, which is nil here). `load()` additionally debounces 0.3s, and `readFailure` is only rewritten when the read settles — so on a persistent lock the click repaints the identical string and literally nothing moves. Every other actionable tier acknowledges the click with \"Fetching…\"/\"Pushing…\"; this one is the only enabled cell in the bar with zero in-flight state.","fix":"Render the read in flight. Either extend `VCSSyncActivity` with a `.reading` case (or pass `isReading: model.state == .loading`) and have [13b] resolve to a disabled \"Trying again…\" + `ProgressView` while it runs, or publish a `readInFlight` flag from `RemoteStateModel.load()` and disable the segment for its duration. Also drop the debounce on a forced refresh so the acknowledgement is immediate.","fingerprint":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Views/VCSToolbar.swift:138:feedback","specialist":"design"}
{"severity":"CRITICAL","confidence":9,"path":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/VCSSyncPresentation.swift","line":430,"category":"copy","summary":"The dialog reached from the new read-failure tier titles itself \"The last action failed\" when no action was attempted. `RemoteStateModel.presentFailureDetails()` raises a read failure with `action: nil`, and `failureDialog` falls back to `title: \"The last action failed\"` — flatly contradicting [13b]'s own comment (\"Deliberately not `lastAction`-labelled: nothing was attempted\"). The new UI test `testAFailedReadCanShowItsDetails` walks exactly this path (right-click → Show Error Details…) and never checks the title. The same dialog also offers no recovery button while the bar behind it says \"Try Again\", so the two surfaces disagree about whether a retry exists.","fix":"Give the dialog a read-failure voice: pass the tier's intent through (e.g. `failureDialog(_:action:workroom:isRead:now:)` or a nil-action branch) and title it \"Couldn’t read the repository\" / \"Reading <workroom> failed\" instead of naming a phantom action. While there, either surface a re-read as the dialog's default button (a non-`VCSRemoteAction` `onRetryRead` closure) or drop \"Try Again\" from the bar for that failure, so the bar and the sheet agree.","fingerprint":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/VCSSyncPresentation.swift:430:copy","specialist":"design"}
{"severity":"INFORMATIONAL","confidence":9,"path":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Views/VCSFailureSheet.swift","line":134,"category":"copy","summary":"`copyReport()` still joins only `[title, message, details]`, so the new \"in <workroom>\" subtitle is dropped from the clipboard — losing the one fact the subtitle was added to preserve, in the output whose documented purpose is \"what you'd paste into an issue or a chat\". A pasted report from a background workroom's failure is therefore indistinguishable from one about the workroom on screen.","fix":"Include it: `let text = [dialog.title, dialog.subtitle, dialog.message, dialog.details].compactMap { $0 }.joined(separator: \"\\n\\n\")` — or join title+subtitle on one line (\"Push failed in platform / fix-auth\") so the paste reads as a heading rather than three stanzas.","fingerprint":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Views/VCSFailureSheet.swift:134:copy","specialist":"design"}
{"severity":"INFORMATIONAL","confidence":7,"path":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/VCSSyncPresentation.swift","line":194,"category":"accessibility","summary":"The spoken label for this enabled button never says what clicking does. VoiceOver gets \"Reading the repository failed. <cause>\" — the word \"Try Again\", the only thing that identifies the control as a retry, exists solely as sighted text (the count pills' precedent shows the label is expected to carry everything visual). Worse for a located lock: `explain` is a multi-paragraph account, so the button's label dictates a file path, an age and a literal `rm \"/…/index.lock\"` command. Tier [13] shares the pattern, but there a no-recovery failure is disabled — here it is a focusable, clickable button.","fix":"Lead the label with the affordance and keep the essay in `help`/the dialog: `accessibility: \"Try again. Reading the repository failed. \\(describe(readFailure))\"`, with `accessibilityValue` carrying nothing extra. Reserve the full `explain` text for the tooltip and the sheet, which can be read and copied.","fingerprint":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/VCSSyncPresentation.swift:194:accessibility","specialist":"design"}
{"severity":"INFORMATIONAL","confidence":7,"path":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/VCSSyncPresentation.swift","line":193,"category":"tooltip","summary":"`help: explain(readFailure)` is byte-identical to the visible subtitle for every read failure except a located lock (`explain` falls through to `describe`), so hovering the cell adds nothing, and it never states that clicking re-reads the repository. Compare tiers [5]/[6] (\"Up to date with origin. Fetched 9 minutes ago. Click to fetch again.\") and [4] (\"Push <branch> to <remote> and start tracking it.\"), where the tooltip explains the click. Given the repo rule that every control carries a meaningful `.help`, a tooltip that only repeats the label is a gap on the one clickable cell of this tier.","fix":"Append the affordance: `help: \"\\(explain(readFailure, now: now))\\n\\nClick to read the repository again.\"` (or \"Click to try reading it again.\"), keeping the cause first so a located lock's path still leads.","fingerprint":"macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/VCSSyncPresentation.swift:193:tooltip","specialist":"design"}

